LOGBOOK.md:34:- REWORK: Timeout races now detach callers promptly while a bounded registry retains, cancels, and reports unfinished injected work until it actually returns. Upload keeps the libssh2 channel state machine actor-owned and applies one absolute deadline across open, source read, bounded drains, writes, EOF, and exit; only the injected source read is detached. External signer work follows the same visible ownership rule instead of making teardown wait indefinitely.
LOGBOOK.md:46:- ROOT CAUSE: Long-lived reads reused the write-credit deadline; the authentication timeout raced a waiter that still joined an independently owned signer; rekey and keepalive deadlines began only after the shared session gate; and canceled upload cleanup inherited task cancellation, causing its cleanup progress handler to close the shared TCP bridge.
LOGBOOK.md:54:- CONFORMANCE: Deterministic loopback regressions prove canceled and timed-out reads leave sibling channels and the session ready; an open times out while rekey is deliberately suspended and a second queued open succeeds afterward; two rekey triggers produce one KEX while the first caller cancels; four concurrent same-channel payloads survive forced bridge backpressure byte-exactly; and a supported-but-disallowed credential algorithm fails before authentication.
LOGBOOK.md:60:- CONFORMANCE: A serialized macOS loopback fixture starts ephemeral OpenSSH with an in-memory P-256 external signer and proves host-policy-before-credential ordering, approved public-key authentication, direct-tcpip echo, concurrent exec opens, exec/stdin upload, server-rekey traffic survival, manual client rekey, keepalive transmission, five connected read/cancel races, and three successful connect/close resource baselines. The four M3 semantics remain explicit `unsupported` reports owned by `TASK-260728-3cveay`.
LOGBOOK.md:66:- REWORK: Upload has an overall deadline and rejects oversized source chunks; timeout racing returns without waiting for a non-cooperative injected dependency. External signer work is explicitly tracked, notification-driven rather than 1 ms polled, cancelled, and joined. Connect failures retain their pre-teardown phase, timeout/cancellation counters reconcile, and automatic keepalive failures consume the configured miss budget before fatal teardown.
LOGBOOK.md:72:- SECURITY: The adapter applies explicit KEX/host-key/cipher/MAC allowlists with no SHA-1/CBC fallback, delivers the exact raw host-key blob plus negotiated host-key method and canonical SHA-256 fingerprint to policy before credential lookup, and carries only opaque credential references/public signing material across Core. Engine prose and endpoint/user/command data never enter errors or typed diagnostics.
LOGBOOK.md:309:- FINDING: The notarization credential was described as "available" while existing only as a mode-0600 `.p8` file — the project invariant is Keychain-only. ADR-025 now requires a named `notarytool` Keychain profile, a real authentication check, and a recorded disposition for the source file; `TASK-260728-dveo1o` owns it and blocks `3gkwn0`.
LOGBOOK.md:331:- DECISION: Codex `gpt-5.6-sol` high as primary orchestrator, Claude `claude-opus-5` as producer, Codex `gpt-5.6-sol` high as independent reviewer, `max_parallel: 1`. Replaces the Fable-orchestrator policy and the 2026-07-20 out-of-credits Claude-only fallback.
LOGBOOK.md:522:- RELIABILITY/CLEANUP: Event traces now cover both IPv4→IPv6 and IPv6→IPv4 orders, cancellation/tombstone/late-response races, duplicate attempts before suppression, every M2 fallback trigger, malformed/mismatched no-shopping, same-endpoint TCP, later promotion, and exact attempt/terminal counts. Transactions, queue bytes, reservations, tombstones, connections, connection buffers, fixed bytes, and descriptors return to observed zero after every regenerated run.
LOGBOOK.md:552:- CORRECTION: The normative ownership sequence now matches `HEVSOCKSBoundary.swift:284-299`: immediately after TCP accept/socket setup, an already-stopped or generation-retired boundary or a full pending-authentication set closes the descriptor without a SOCKS5 method reply, RFC 1929 reply, authentication enqueue, or adapter handoff.
LOGBOOK.md:553:- BOUNDARY: Wrong/stale capability and the M1 monotonic accept-to-auth deadline remain authentication-phase failures with only phase-and-remaining-budget-safe replies. The post-handoff adapter resource reservation is separate from the boundary pending-authentication ceiling.
LOGBOOK.md:558:- CORRECTION: Current `HEVSOCKSBoundary` uses `SO_RCVTIMEO`, which is a per-receive inactivity bound and can restart as bytes arrive; authentication sends have no deadline. The pending set is count-bounded, but current source does not prove an absolute accept-to-auth deadline. M1 must compute one monotonic deadline at accept, apply its remaining budget across greeting/auth reads, comparisons, and replies without progress extension, and prove slow-trickle/reply-stall eviction plus slot/descriptor release on iOS and macOS.
