 ## 2026-08-10
 
+### 2155 — Review: mandatory Ed25519 and automatic-rekey rows lack positive adapter evidence (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
+- REVIEW: Changes requested after the round-10 ownership race was independently cleared: three consecutive `swift test --filter LibSSH2` runs pass 41 tests/3 suites, and the full core, pinned-source, tamper, Apple matrix, lint, diff, and board gates all exit 0.
+- GAP: The revised M0 contract requires noninteractive Ed25519 plus an approved fallback through the opaque external signer. The live adapter fixture authenticates only with an in-memory P-256 signer; the pinned C rekey probe uses file-based Ed25519 auth and therefore does not exercise the adapter/Keychain signer boundary. A scoped search for an Ed25519 live-auth credential in `LibSSH2AdapterIntegrationTests.swift` exits 1.
+- GAP: Client rekey requires byte-threshold, time-threshold, test, and manual triggers on the production KEX path under active traffic. Integration tests cover manual/test callers and server `RekeyLimit`, but configure the adapter byte threshold to `UInt64.max` and elapsed threshold to 3,600 seconds. A scoped search for `.byteThreshold`, `.timeThreshold`, `clientByteRekeys`, or `clientTimeRekeys` assertions in the adapter tests exits 1.
+- REWORK: Add deterministic live adapter coverage for Ed25519 external signing and for both automatic rekey triggers under traffic, asserting KEX success, trigger counters/events, channel survival, bounded cancellation/close, and zero owned-resource baseline. If either path fails, fix the adapter rather than reporting the mandatory row green.
+
 ### 2144 — libssh2 upload timeout exposes deterministic ownership (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
 - ROOT CAUSE: The timeout race resumed its public continuation before cancelling the losing child, and the upload path returned after cancelling cooperative stdout/stderr work without waiting for those timeout-race records to retire. Depending on scheduling, the post-timeout snapshot contained the one intentionally non-cooperative upload source plus transient cooperative children; an unbounded test poll could then turn the ownership mismatch into a hung combined gate.
 - REWORK: The race now signals cancellation before resuming its caller. The bounded ownership registry supports count-targeted retirement waiters, and a timed-out upload gives cooperative children at most 250 ms of the injected close budget to reconcile while permitting exactly one additional operation—the cancellation-ignoring source—to remain visible until release. The regression uses bounded monotonic state synchronization and fails instead of hanging if ownership cannot settle.

